# CLASS: conflicting-signal (library convention, 2c) — CONTESTED convention test for the
#        design rule "only policy that contradicts the training prior discriminates":
#        canonical answer for a read/refresh trigger is switchMap (cancel stale), reinforced
#        by neighbor typeahead.js; team policy is exhaustMap (ignore refresh spam).
# GAP: "refresh/reload triggers use exhaustMap ... switchMap is for typeahead queries only" (configs/js-rxjs-refresh-b/CLAUDE.md)
# HYPOTHESIS: A picks switchMap (canonical for reads + neighbor pattern) or mergeMap — both
#             start/restart a load on the spam click and fail the hidden ignore-in-flight test
TASK_ID="js-rxjs-refresh-015"
PROMPT="Implement refreshData(clicks\$, loadFn) in src/refresh.js: clicks\$ emits when the user clicks Refresh, loadFn() returns an Observable that performs one dashboard load; the returned Observable emits the loaded dashboard data. Follow the project's RxJS conventions. Make npm test pass; do not modify the tests."
FIXTURE="js-rxjs-refresh"
CONFIG="js-rxjs-refresh-b"
HIDDEN="js-rxjs-refresh-hidden"
MAX_TURNS="12"
ALLOWED_TOOLS="Read,Edit,Write,Glob,Grep,Bash(node:*),Bash(npm:*)"
CHECK="check.sh"
